        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(vault): aggregate provider outage diagnostics",
        "body": "Closes #110859\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using Vault-backed SecretRefs would receive one repeated provider-authentication diagnostic per affected owner during a Vault outage, obscuring the shared cause and producing noisy startup reports.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nVault resolution now distinguishes provider-wide availability or authentication failures from path-specific reference failures. Runtime startup carries that provider provenance internally and emits one provider diagnostic with the complete affected-owner list, while preserving per-reference isolation for ACL failures and mixed batches. Bounded response parsing and a self-token check classify Vault's standard revoked-token 403 without exposing values or reference identifiers.\n\nVault grants `auth/token/lookup-self` through its default policy. The Vault guide now documents the equivalent explicit capability for operators who intentionally create no-default-policy tokens, because Vault uses the same bare 403 for expired tokens and callers denied access to that endpoint.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDuring a Vault/provider outage, operators now see one actionable `SECRETS_PROVIDER_DEGRADED` diagnostic per failed provider and the affected owners. Path-specific permission failures remain isolated when token introspection succeeds, and mixed success/failure batches retain usable values.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Real Gateway startup proof: actual Vault resolver wrapper, two affected owners, one resolver process, one provider diagnostic, and `/readyz` HTTP 200.\n- ACL boundary proof: Vault path 403 plus successful `lookup-self` remains per-reference; Vault's standard revoked-token 403 plus `lookup-self` 403 becomes one provider failure.\n- Focused remote proof: 91 tests passed across Vault resolution, runtime fan-out/warnings, and Gateway startup diagnostics/owner isolation.\n- Post-review focused proof: Vault resolver 26/26 and real Gateway owner-isolation 10/10 passed.\n- Full remote `pnpm check:changed`: passed, including format, type lanes, lint, boundary guards, and changed-surface checks.\n- Fresh autoreview against current `origin/main`: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Blacksmith Testbox proof: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29656447677\n\nAI-assisted implementation. I reviewed the behavior, tests, upstream Vault token-policy contract, and resulting diff.\n",
